# Same range cuts as the DC3/DC4 sources (optimizes sim time):
DefaultRangeCut 0.005
Region Spacecraft
Spacecraft.Volume SCbody
Spacecraft.RangeCut 1.

Region Pipebody
Pipebody.Volume PIPbody
Pipebody.RangeCut 1.

DetectorTimeConstant 0.000002

# Local particle event: quasi-trapped electrons, exp(-E/200 keV),
# peak I(>30 keV) = 140 e/cm2/s/sr at 90 deg pitch, sin^4 pitch-angle distribution.
# Rocking -21.88 deg, yaw 59.97 deg, field dip 0 deg. Directions in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source LOCLPAR0001
LOCLPAR0001.ParticleType 3
LOCLPAR0001.Beam FarFieldNormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction LOCLPAR0001_beam.dat
LOCLPAR0001.Spectrum NormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835944184.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_1sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curve (absolute unix times): LOCLPAR0001_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
LOCLPAR0001.Lightcurve File false LOCLPAR0001_lightcurve_shifted.dat
